## Summary
Add `kernel_wkv7_f32_masked` that accepts sequence lengths and skips state updates for padding positions, preserving the invariant `h(seq + padding) == h(seq)`.

## Context
The current WKV7 kernel requires all sequences to have equal length. Naive padding corrupts state because the update `state = state * w + sa * b + k * v` always adds `k * v`.

**Why length-masking works for RWKV7:**
- State lives in thread registers (fast)
- Timesteps processed sequentially within each thread
- Simple branch to skip padding has minimal overhead

## Implementation
**File:** `src/hip/kernels/copy.hip`

```cpp
__global__ void kernel_wkv7_f32_masked(
    const float* __restrict__ w_decay,
    const float* __restrict__ q,
    const float* __restrict__ k,
    const float* __restrict__ v,
    const float* __restrict__ a,
    const float* __restrict__ b,
    const float* __restrict__ state_in,
    float* __restrict__ output,
    float* __restrict__ state_out,
    const int* __restrict__ lengths,  // NEW: [B] real sequence length per batch
    int N, int H, int T, int B
) {
    int bb = blockIdx.y;
    int real_len = lengths[bb];

    // ... existing state init ...

    for (int t = 0; t < T; t++) {
        // ... existing shared memory loads ...

        if (t < real_len) {
            // Normal state update (existing code)
            float v_val = v[ind];
            // ... sa computation ...
            for (int j = 0; j < WKV7_HEAD_SIZE; j++) {
                state[j] = state[j] * sh_w[j] + sa * sh_b[j] + sh_k[j] * v_val;
            }
            // ... output computation ...
            output[ind] = y;
        }
        // For padding positions: state unchanged, output undefined
    }

    // Save final state (same as before)
}

hipError_t launch_wkv7_f32_masked(
    /* existing params */,
    const int* lengths,
    /* N, H, T, B */,
    hipStream_t stream
);
```

