## Summary
Add `forward_with_state_masked()` to `Rwkv7Hip` that accepts padded tokens and real lengths, using the length-masked WKV7 kernel.

## Context
This bridges the gap between the HIP kernel (which needs lengths) and the runtime (which has variable-length batches).

## Implementation
**File:** `src/hip/mod.rs`

```rust
impl Rwkv7Hip {
    /// Forward pass with length masking for variable-length batches.
    /// 
    /// # Arguments
    /// * `tokens` - Padded token sequences, all same length T
    /// * `lengths` - Real sequence length per batch (lengths[b] <= T)
    /// * `state` - Mutable state, updated in place
    /// 
    /// # Returns
    /// Logits tensor [vocab_size, T, B] - only positions < lengths[b] are valid
    pub fn forward_with_state_masked(
        &self,
        tokens: &[&[u32]],      // All same length (padded)
        lengths: &[usize],      // Real length per batch
        state: &mut HipState,
    ) -> Result<Vec<f32>> {
        let batch_size = tokens.len();
        let max_len = tokens[0].len();

        // Validate
        assert!(tokens.iter().all(|t| t.len() == max_len));
        assert!(lengths.len() == batch_size);
        assert!(lengths.iter().all(|&l| l <= max_len));

        // ... existing embedding, layer processing ...

        // For WKV7: use masked kernel
        let lengths_gpu = self.upload_lengths(lengths)?;
        launch_wkv7_f32_masked(
            /* existing params */,
            lengths_gpu.as_ptr(),
            N, H, T, B,
            stream
        )?;

        // ... continue with existing logic ...
    }

    fn upload_lengths(&self, lengths: &[usize]) -> Result<DeviceBuffer<i32>> {
        let lengths_i32: Vec<i32> = lengths.iter().map(|&l| l as i32).collect();
        DeviceBuffer::from_slice(&lengths_i32)
    }
}
