## Proposed Test: Teacher Forcing Equivalence

The key test should:
1. **Prefill with EOS token only** (single token, initializes state)
2. **Decode remaining tokens one-by-one** using teacher forcing (ground truth tokens)
3. **Compare against prefill of full sequence**

```rust
#[test]
fn test_decode_state_equivalence() {
    let model = load_model();
    let tokens = [EOS, tok1, tok2, tok3, ..., tokN];

    // Path A: Prefill entire sequence
    let mut state_prefill = HipState::new(&model.info, 1);
    let logits_prefill = model.forward_with_state(&[&tokens], &mut state_prefill)?;

    // Path B: Prefill EOS only, then decode rest one-by-one
    let mut state_decode = HipState::new(&model.info, 1);
    let _ = model.forward_with_state(&[&[EOS]], &mut state_decode)?;  // Prefill EOS

    let mut logits_decode = Vec::new();
    for &tok in &tokens[1..] {
        let logits = model.forward_with_state(&[&[tok]], &mut state_decode)?;
        logits_decode.extend(logits);
    }

    // Both paths should produce identical results
    assert_tensors_close(&logits_prefill[vocab_size..], &logits_decode, rtol, atol);
    assert_states_close(&state_prefill, &state_decode, rtol, atol);
}
```

